From 19b87328d1bd0b7b120d43d719af8fa1af492068 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:24:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Patch 0169: OPTIONS as switches, with DIGITAL CLOCK, NEW
 STATUS BARS and FRAME RATE

The OPTIONS box has four rows, each a label and its two values side by side, the chosen one
yellow and the other grey: JAPANESE CONTROLS OFF/ON, DIGITAL CLOCK OFF/ON (0166's plate,
default on), NEW STATUS BARS OFF/ON (0162-0164's fill; off draws the original's bars, default
on) and FRAME RATE 30/60 FPS (default the build's, 60). Left picks the left value, right the
right one, confirm the other one. With FPS=30|60 MOD_FPS_MODE is the run-time MOD_FPS_MODE_RUN
(dw/mod_fps.h); FPS=20 keeps the compile-time 0. SAVE_TAG_OPTIONS grows to 4 bytes (buttons,
clock, frame rate 30/60, bars); a shorter record leaves the rest at their defaults.

